# Configuration example for sqlite-mcp-server.
#
# The server does NOT auto-load .env files (no dotenv dependency) — it reads
# process.env directly. Copy this file to .env and export its contents before
# starting the server, e.g.:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#   npm start
#
# Alternatively, pass the same value as the first CLI argument instead of
# setting DB_PATH, or set it directly in your MCP host's server config
# (see README.md → Connect to agent).

# Path to the SQLite database file. Absolute, or relative to this project's
# root (the directory containing package.json) — NOT relative to whatever
# directory the process happens to be launched from.
DB_PATH=../sqlitedb/shop.db
